- op: discuss  # f05e
  at: '2026-07-17T20:14:54Z'  # f05e
  by: agent  # f05e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f05e
  clock: 9  # f05e
  nonce: f05e  # f05e
  message: "WONT_DO per fundamental-concept-audit KEEP verdict (2026-07-17; owner-approved Option A after a 3-lens ADR/spec/spirit investigation). The premise INVERTED since filing: the entrypoint detector no longer uses a private narrow test_*.py check but the SHARED BROAD paths.is_test_file heuristic (test-OR-support: also mocks/fixtures/testdata/benches/_test.<any-ext>/spec_*), while canonical Symbol.is_test_file is the NARROW supply-chain role flag (test *code* only, spec §14; ADR-0041 §1 deliberately excludes fuzz/bench). The two are distinct-purpose predicates -- all four leakage tests pass -> KEEP -- NOT a coarse-vs-granular pair. The entrypoint predicate is BROADER, so it is OUTSIDE META-bifif's 're-derive coarser' invariant; swapping onto is_test_file would silently stop deprioritizing mock/fixture/benchmark entrypoints (empirical divergence at mocks/, foo_test.ts, etc.). Behavioral evidence: guard test test_support_dir_entrypoint_penalized_via_broad_path_heuristic (merged 47878acd82) -- a mocks/ main STAYS penalized; its classify_file(...).is_test is False assertion is the executable re-eval trigger. Documented at the penalty site + both boundary docstrings (disambiguated the two 'canonical' labels), ADR-0041 §2 annotated in place (directness ruling unaffected), CHANGELOG. Full audit: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-is_test_file_07172026.md. Re-eval triggers: (1) canonical is_test broadens to the support breadth; (2) a consumer needs the two to agree and divergence causes a measured misclassification; (3) >5 entrypoint-bearing divergent files on a single repo. Advances INV-numat drain; removes a false META-bifif member."  # f05e
